KZ2 patch 6042: the lv2 syscalls' condition variables on ps3_evcv (patch 6041) instead of the Win32
CONDITION_VARIABLE: sys_mutex (lock with a timeout sleeps in 1 ms slices), sys_event_queue receive (timed and the
EVT_RECV_KICK wait; sys_timer's push wakes the same cv), sys_event_flag wait (timed), sys_cond wait (timed), and the
SPU port-bind wait in lv2_register (sys_spu_thread_send_event before the PPU has connected the port, up to
SPU_PORT_BIND_WAIT_MS). Each of these timed waits went through ntdll's RtlWaitOnAddress under Wine, whose futex queue
corrupts itself when a timeout meets a wake (patch 6041's header). The untimed waits on the same objects move with
them (one type per object). Same behaviour otherwise; the pthread branches are unchanged.

